🌐 Graphs in Java

A collection of Graph Data Structure implementations and problems solved using Java. This folder covers graph creation, traversal algorithms, and path-finding techniques.

📚 Topics Covered

🔹 Graph Basics

- Creating a Graph
- Graph Representation using Adjacency List

🔹 Graph Traversal

- Breadth First Search (BFS)
- Depth First Search (DFS)

🔹 Graph Problems

- Has Path Problem (Path Existence using DFS)

💡 Concepts Used

- Graph Data Structure
- Vertices and Edges
- Adjacency List
- ArrayList
- Queue
- Recursion
- Stack
- Visited Array

💻 Technologies Used

- Java
- Data Structures & Algorithms

🎯 Learning Goals

- Understand graph representation.
- Learn BFS and DFS traversal.
- Understand path finding in graphs.
- Improve problem-solving and logical thinking.

